---
/**
 * Site header.
 *
 * NO JAVASCRIPT, AND NO MOBILE MENU COMPONENT.
 *
 * The constitution says a hydration directive is only justified when the
 * interaction cannot reasonably be built from native HTML and CSS. The two
 * primary links fit on a small screen unaided, so there is nothing to
 * disclose, let alone anything needing JS to disclose it.
 *
 * THE SOCIAL ROW USED TO BE HIDDEN BELOW `md`, AND NOW IT IS NOT. As words --
 * "LINKEDIN INSTAGRAM FACEBOOK" -- it cost about 250px and wrapped a 375px
 * phone to three lines, so it was hidden, and a phone reader never saw the
 * profiles at all. That was the honest trade at the time and it was also the
 * wrong outcome: supplementary is not the same as invisible.
 *
 * As glyphs the same three cost 80px, and the theme toggle giving up its
 * "DARK"/"LIGHT" text freed another 31px. The header now holds all of it on
 * ONE line from 375px up, which covers every current iPhone and Pixel. Below
 * that -- 360px Androids and the 320px long tail -- it wraps to two lines,
 * 72px instead of 51px, and the socials still show. That is a deliberate
 * choice to spend 21px of sticky chrome rather than hide the links again.
 *
 * EVERY BREAKPOINT IN THIS FILE IS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED, and the numbers go
 * stale the moment a label changes. Re-measure before trusting one.
 *
 * If the PRIMARY nav ever outgrows its line, the next step is a native
 * <details>/<summary> disclosure -- still zero JS. An island is the last
 * resort, not the first.
 */
import SocialIcon from '../ui/SocialIcon.astro';
import ThemeToggle from '../ui/ThemeToggle.astro';
import { primaryNav } from '../../data/navigation';
import { person } from '../../data/person';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../../data/site';
import { isActivePath } from '../../utils/urls';

const current = Astro.url.pathname;
---

{/*
  The hairline is full-strength ink, not a polite grey. See DESIGN.md -- a 1px
  full-contrast rule is the most characteristic mark in the system, and
  softening borders is the fastest route back to a generic site.
*/}
{/*
  Sticky so navigation stays reachable through a long article. It was
  originally made sticky to host a reading-progress bean that rolled along the
  bottom hairline; that moved to the brew column in the margin, but keeping
  the nav in reach on a page you scroll for several screens stands on its own.
*/}
<header class="sticky top-0 z-50 border-b border-line bg-surface">
  <div
    class="mx-auto flex max-w-wide flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-2 gap-y-2 px-gutter py-3 md:gap-x-4"
  >
    <a
      href="/"
      class="font-mono text-kicker font-normal tracking-[0.08em] text-ink uppercase no-underline"
    >
      {SITE_NAME}
    </a>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-2 md:gap-x-6">
      <nav aria-label="Primary">
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 md:gap-x-6">
        {
          primaryNav.map((item) => {
            const active = isActivePath(item.href, current);
            return (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={item.href}
                  aria-current={active ? 'page' : undefined}
                  class:list={[
                    'font-mono text-kicker tracking-[0.08em] uppercase no-underline hover:text-accent-hover',
                    /*
                     * The current page is marked by an underline as well as by
                     * colour. Colour is never the only carrier of meaning.
                     */
                    active
                      ? 'text-ink underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4'
                      : 'text-ink-muted',
                  ]}
                >
                  {item.label}
                </a>
              </li>
            );
          })
        }
        </ul>
      </nav>

      {
        /*
          Visible at every width -- see the note at the top of this file for
          why these are glyphs rather than the words they replaced.

          The hairline separator and its padding are `md` and up only: on a
          phone that 24px of inset is the difference between one line and two,
          and at that width the icons read as a group without help.

          Separated from the primary nav by an ink hairline rather than by
          extra space. DESIGN.md says to separate with whitespace first and
          stop as soon as it reads, but at this density it did not read: the
          two navs are the same size, weight and case, so a wider gap looked
          like an uneven gap rather than a boundary. A 1px full-strength rule
          is the next step and the most characteristic mark in the system.

          These are external and can never be the current page, so unlike the
          primary nav there is no aria-current or active treatment here.

          rel="me" repeats the footer's identity claim. Asserting it twice on
          one page is harmless -- verifiers look for the link, not for exactly
          one of it -- and omitting it on the more prominent of the two
          placements would be the odd choice.
        */
      }
      {
        person.socialProfiles.length > 0 && (
          <nav aria-label="Social profiles" class="md:border-l md:border-line md:pl-6">
            <ul class="flex items-center gap-x-1 md:gap-x-2">
              {person.socialProfiles.map((profile) => (
                <li>
                  <a
                    href={profile.url}
                    rel="me noopener"
                    class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center text-ink-muted no-underline hover:text-accent-hover"
                  >
                    <SocialIcon name={profile.label} />
                    <span class="sr-only">{profile.label}</span>
                  </a>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </nav>
        )
      }

      {
        /*
          FORK THIS SITE. The one call to action in the header, which is why it
          is styled as a bordered box rather than carried in `primaryNav` with
          the other links -- and why it has no `aria-current`. It is an action,
          not a location.

          A BORDERED LINK, NOT AN ACCENT FILL. DESIGN.md keeps the accent for
          links, the focus ring and a selected state, "not a button fill on
          every button". Colour comes from `.kicker` plus a `text-ink`
          override, the same move as ThemeToggle.

          HIDDEN BELOW `md`, AND THE BREAKPOINT IS MEASURED. It used to be
          `lg`, because the socials were three WORDS at roughly 250px and this
          button pushed 768px to a second line. They are glyphs now, at 113px,
          and the toggle lost its text as well, so 768px went from 0px of slack
          to 315px and the old reason stopped being true. Measured again rather
          than inherited.

          Below `md` it still does not fit, and the footer carries the same
          destination at every width, which is what makes hiding it honest. On
          a phone the homepage hero carries it too.

          It points at /open-source/, not at GitHub; that file's header
          explains why.
        */
      }
      <a
        href="/open-source/"
        class="kicker hidden border border-line px-3 py-1 text-ink no-underline md:inline-block hover:border-accent hover:text-accent-hover"
      >
        Fork this site
      </a>

      <ThemeToggle />
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
